ment, as well as being used for monitoring during therapy and surveillance/follow-up after treatment (including examples referencing cancer contexts). This indicates the community’s relevance to decision-making across the care continuum, from initial detection to longitudinal monitoring. [Data: Entities (82)]\\n\\nBecause the community describes common clinical practices rather than illicit activity, its “impact” is primarily informational and operational: it outlines a structured set of examination components and techniques that shape subsequent diagnostic and management decisions (e.g., when findings prompt further evaluation). The network’s impact is therefore moderate as a foundational clinical workflow rather than a high-severity risk cluster. [Data: Entities (82, 5221, 1466); Relationships (11546, 7668, 12100)]\"}],\"rating\":3.1,\"rating_explanation\":\"Impact is low-to-moderate because the community describes routine, widely used clinical examination components and techniques that influence care decisions but do not indicate elevated risk, wrongdoing, or adversarial capability. [Data: Entities (82, 5221, 1466); Relationships (11546, 7668)]\"}", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, "provider_specific_fields": {"native_finish_reason": "stop"}}], "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1791, "prompt_tokens": 4107, "total_tokens": 5898, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null, "text_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1664, "text_tokens": null, "image_tokens": null}}, "service_tier": null}}}